# Frames are large and REPRODUCIBLE from the source video with tools/dji_stills.py
# + vision/make_split.py. The LABELS beside them are hand-drawn and are not
# reproducible by anything, so those stay tracked.
#
# One file here rather than one per dataset: a per-dataset .gitignore has to be
# remembered every time a new set is made, and the first time it is forgotten a
# few hundred MB of JPEGs land in the history where they cannot be removed
# without a rewrite.
images/
*/images/
*/review/
*/preview/
*/check/
*/pending/
*/excluded_oblique/
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.cache

# Merged sets are DERIVED: `merge_datasets.py` rebuilds them byte-identically
# from the source sets (verified 2026-08-22). Tracking them would duplicate every
# label file and create two places for the same truth to drift apart.
dji_merged/
*_merged/

# Generated tool PAGES (label_bays.py / align_bays.py): a few MB each of frames
# embedded as base64, rebuilt from the stills in seconds. The labels a human
# produces IN them are the irreplaceable part, and those are the exported
# gt_*.json / align_*.json / bay_outlines.json, which stay tracked.
gt_*.html
align_*.html
*.dets.json
